Rāma meets huge vulture en route --- Vulture calls himself father friend --- Rāma asks his lineage and name --- Jaṭāyu recounts Prajāpatis Dakṣa daughters Kaśyapa unions --- Jaṭāyu traces dēvas daityas birds beasts humans nāgas births --- Jaṭāyu names himself Aruṇa son Śyēnī child --- Jaṭāyu offers to guard Sītā in absence --- Rāma embraces Jaṭāyu and reaches Pañcavaṭī